  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH Response in Gambella- ETH: Strengthening Innovation and Sustainability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This fund match -funds projects, leveraging new donor income for Oxfam innovations. To date, Pioneers have supported over 76 innovation projects globally, with more in development. The Global Humanitarian Team (GHT) Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) Team conducts annual calls for proposals across Oxfam country teams, focusing on specific WASH challenges. This provides staff and partners with opportunities to innovate and test approaches in diverse contexts. These projects benefit both Oxfam&apos;s programming and the broader WASH sector. Learning is disseminated through reports, blogs, presentations, and peer -to -peer exchanges facilitated by Humanitarian Support Personnel. Furthermore, WASH innovation projects funded by Pioneers have been presented at external global learning events like the Emergency Environmental Health Forum, contributing to the global WASH sector.</narrative>
  </description>
